task_id: sql_0022
task_type: sql
instruction: "The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show the price of the most expensive ware for each category (the maximal price among all product records of the wares in the category). The result should be ordered by the category. Write one row per line as category;price, the price rounded to one decimal point. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt)."
reward: 2
expected: "Chemicals;25.8\nFood;44.9\nFuel;25.8\nLivestock;149.5\nMineral;14.8\nRaw food;14.9\nRaw material;14.9\nReady food;44.9\nStuff;1299.7"
check: exact_str